<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11244" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrōnēa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κορώνεια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Bœotia, west of Lake
			Copais</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Ages. 4, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 33,
				29, 6</span></i> and 9 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence the <i>adjj.</i>,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrōnaeus</span></b> 
			or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ēus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Coronea</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					36, 20, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrōnensis</span></b> , e, the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					36, 20, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
